"1st"}},{"id":"401892445000000790","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":0,"text":"Brayden Point faceoff won against Trevor Zegras","type":{"id":"502","text":"Face Off","abbreviation":"faceoff"},"clock":{"displayValue":"1:46"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"20"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"3151187","displayName":"Brayden Point","shortName":"B. Point"},"type":"face-off-winner"},{"athlete":{"id":"4565230","displayName":"Trevor Zegras","shortName":"T. Zegras"}}]},{"id":"401892445000000860","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":0,"text":"J.J. Moser Snap Shot High and Wide Left","type":{"id":"507","text":"Missed","abbreviation":"shot-missed"},"clock":{"displayValue":"2:19"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"20"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"4874929","displayName":"J.J. Moser","shortName":"J.J. Moser"},"type":"shooter"},{"athlete":{"id":"3942459","displayName":"Dan Vladar","shortName":"D. Vladar"}}]}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"1396","guid":"713cae18-f94f-330c-ab1a-eb284df12c97","fullName":"Benchmark International Arena","address":{"city":"Tampa","state":"FL","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1396.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":19092,"officials":[{"fullName":"Shandor Alphonso","displayName":"Shandor Alphonso","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Garrett Rank","displayName":"Garrett Rank","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Beau Halkidis","displayName":"Beau Halkidis","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Kyle Flemington","displayName":"Kyle Flemington","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Lightning roll past the winless Flyers 4-1 as Vasilevskiy ties Andy Moog on career wins list","description":"— Pontus Holmberg and Ilya Mikheyev each had a goal and assist, Andrei Vasilevskiy stopped 13 shots to move into a tie for 20th place on the NHL career wins list,...","story":"TAMPA, Fla. -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4588205/pontus-holmberg\">Pontus Holmberg</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4422415/ilya-mikheyev\">Ilya Mikheyev</a> each had a goal and assist, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2976847/andrei-vasilevskiy\">Andrei Vasilevskiy</a> stopped 13 shots to move into a tie for 20th place on the <a href=\"https://records.nhl.com/records/goaltender-records/wins/most-wins-career\">NHL career wins list</a>, and the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/tb/tampa-bay-lightning\">Tampa Bay Lightning</a> beat the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/phi/philadelphia-flyers\">Philadelphia Flyers</a> 4-1 on Monday night.\n\n\r\n              Vasilevskiy's 372nd victory moved him into a tie with Andy Moog. Vasilevskiy needs two more wins to tie John Vanbiesbrouck for 19th place.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3151187/brayden-point\">Brayden Point</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4065019/brandon-hagel\">Brandon Hagel</a> also scored for the Lightning, who have won two games since an opening-night loss to the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/nyr/new-york-rangers\">New York Rangers</a>.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697406/tyson-foerster\">Tyson Foerster</a> scored for Philadelphia and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3942459/dan-vladar\">Dan Vladar</a> finished with 32 saves.\n\n\r\n              The Flyers are winless (0-2-2) through four games to start the season for the first time since 2013-14. Philadelphia has been held to two or fewer goals in all four games.\n\n\r\n              Point scored his first goal of the season with a deflection off a wrist shot from <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5118/john-carlson\">John Carlson</a> at 16:05 of the first period. Holmberg scored 17 seconds into the second period off the rush for a 2-0 lead.\n\n\r\n              Foerster wheeled a shot from the top of the left circle that hit Tampa Bay defenseman <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4588175/charle-edouard-d'astous\">Charle-Edouard D'Astous</a> in front of the net to bring Philadelphia with one at 7:22.\n\n\r\n              Mikheyev made it 3-1 with a wraparound with three minutes to play. Hagel added an empty-netter.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2563060/nikita-kucherov\">Nikita Kucherov</a> picked up two assists and now has 1,128 career points to move past Mike Bossy and Joe Nieuwendyk for 67th place.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5173105/denver-barkey\">Denver Barkey</a> made his season debut for the Flyers after missing the first three games with an undisclosed lower-body injury.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up Next</hl2>\r\n              Flyers: At <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/ott/ottawa-senators\">Ottawa Senators</a> on Thursday night.\n\n\r\n              Lightning: Host <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/min/minnesota-wild\">Minnesota Wild</a> on Thursday night.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-10-06T02:14:27Z"}}